<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salehuddin of Selangor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1778</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Raja Lumu, Sultan Salehuddin Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salehuddin of Selangor, born Raja Lumu, was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Selangor, recognised around 1766 with the sanction of the ruler of Perak. A son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daeng-chelak">Daeng Chelak</a>, he ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuala-selangor">Kuala Selangor</a> and turned the Bugis settlements on the Selangor coast into a sultanate. His descendants still hold the throne.</p></div>
